A: The basic idea of OpenMP is to distribute work. For this you need to create some threads. The parallel construct creates this number of threads. Afterwards you can distibute/share work with other constructs like omp for or omp task . A possible benefit of this distinction is e.g. when you have to allocate memory for each thread (i.e. thread-local data).
