A: You should profile it and check where threads spend time. One possible reason is that parallel regions are constantly created and destroyed; depending on OpenMP implementation, it could lead to re-creation of the thread pool, though good implementations should probably handle this case. Some small things to shave off: - ok seems completely unnecessary, you can just change the loop exit condition to i<n-1 ; - explicit barrier is unnecessary - first, you put it out of parallel regions so it makes no sense; and second, OpenMP parallel regions and loops have implicit barriers at the end; - combine at least the two consequent parallel regions inside the while loop: #pragma omp parallel private(tmp)
