A: I've tried many options, including using tasks instead of sections (with the same results), switching compilers, etc. As suggested by Qubit, I also tried to use std::async. This was the solution! The CPU usage dropped from about 50% to 30% (this is on a different computer from the original post, so the numbers are different -- it's a 1.5x performance gain for 1.6x CPU usage basically). This is much closer to what I expected for this computer. For reference, here is the new code outline: void SimulationManager::runParallel(){
