A: Of course race conditions can slow the code down. When two or more threads access the same part of memory (same cache line), that part must be loaded into the cache of the given cores over and over again  as the the other thread invalidates the content of the cache by writing into it. They compete for a shared resource. When two variables located too close in memory are written and read by more threads, it also results in a slowdown. This is known as false sharing . In your case it is even worse, they are not just too close, they even coincide.
