A: The likelihood is that this has to do with the ordering of the floating point operations. We all rely on our operations being associative and commutative, but the unfortunate truth is that floating point operations aren't commutative so when they are parallelized, the results may vary because the order gets randomized. Try running your loops backwards and seeing if the result differs. If you do have per thread needs, OMP provides guarantees about iterations of loops falling on the same threads, i.e. if you loop is from 1 to N on a quad core, iterations 1 to N/4 will be run on the same thread. -Rick
