A: The OpenMP 3.1 standard prescribes a very strict form for the for-loop construct (see pag.39): for (init-expr; test-expr; incr-expr) structured-block In particular, test-expr must look like one of the following: var relational-op b
b relational-op var where relational-op is one of <,<=,>,>= and b is a loop invariant expressions of a type compatible with the type of var. Other than that you must ensure that: The values of the loop control expressions of the loops associated
  with the loop  construct must be the same for all the threads in the
  team. So, coming back to your case, I would check sqrtt to be a loop invariant and to have the same value for all threads. A little side note long long isn't standard in C++ prior to C++11, see for instance this question on SO.
