A: Even if your program benefits from using OpenMP, you won't see it because you are measuring the wrong time. clock() returns the total CPU time spent in all threads . If you run with four threads and each runs for 1/4 of the time, clock() will still return the same value since 4*(1/4) = 1. You should be measuring the wall-clock time instead. Replace calls to clock() with omp_get_wtime() or gettimeofday() . They both provide high precision wall-clock timing. P.S. Why are there so many people around SO using clock() for timing?
