A: Floating point addition is neither associative nor commutative! This means that the exact value you obtain depends on the order in which the components of p_sum / sum are added up. To understand precisely why you have to understand how floating point addition works in practice. I would recommend reading What Every Computer Scientist should Know About Floating-Point Arithmetic .
