A: Within the for loop all threads are busy with loop iterations, so there are no resources left to execute stuff in side an iteration in parallel. And in case the work is well balanced you won't gain any better performance. If it is hard/impossible to well-balance the work with a parallel for. You can try generating tasks within the loop, and do the work afterwords. But be aware of the overhead of task generation. #pragma omp parallel private(a,b) shared(f)
{
     #pragma omp for nowait
      for(...)
     {
      //some operations

      #pragma omp task
      {
      int x=func1(a,b);
      int val1=validate(x);
      }

      #pragma omp task
      {
      int y=func2(a,b);
      int val2=validate(y);
      }

     }

     // wait for all tasks to be finished (implicit at the end of the parallel region (here))
     #pragma omp taskwait      
}

