}
pi *= 4*step; As I already stated, induction is the only case I can think of where you need to do this. Your code also saves the result of the reduction per thread. The only reason I can think of doing this is if the operation you are doing is not commutative . Matrix multiplication is not commutative as A*B is not equal to B*A in general. But your operation is commutative but let assume it's not.  In that case you could do the reduction like this double pi = 0.0;
