A: Each j+1 depends on j and j-1 so the j loop has to be sequential: use that as outer loop, and not parallel. However, [i][j+1] does not depend on any other [i+whatever][j+1] so the i iterations can be done in parallel: have the i loop as inner, and make it parallel. (And please put the loop variables in the header: for (int i=whatever) . Declaring everything up front is bad style, and with OpenMP it easily leads to errors.)
