A: You are creating a new bunch of threads each time the while loop gets entered. After the parallel loop, the threads are destroyed. Because of the nature of a while loop, this might happen irregularily (depending on the condition).
So if your loops gets executed only a few times, then the thread creation process might overweigh the actual workload and thus you get at most sequential performance, if not less. However, maybe the parallel system (OpenMP) can detect if the loop is entered many times to keep threads alive. Nothing guaranteed though.
