    #pragma omp parallel for private(j) reduction(+: Wr) private(Omega)
    {
        for( i = 0 ; i < iS- (3) ; i++ ) Note that reduction on Omega makes absolutely no sense, it should be private instead. Also it makes little sense to allocate memory for the full matrices, when you only use columns of them within each iteration. Just make a suitable private datastructure to hold the column(i/j) contents in the first place.

