A: Total memory bandwidth is limited, when you have data bigger than your cache (and 1 GB of data is surely going out of your cache) and a bad access pattern (and sort generally is quite bad, especially the first steps) memory speed is going to be your limit. If you are already capping it with one core, sorting N copies of it in parallel is going to slow it down N times - possibly more as you are also thrashing the L3 cache (each core is trying to access unrelated data).
