} //end parallel Two issues there:
This may result in the threads being unbalanced, if some clusters are significantly bigger than others. This could be solved by counting cluster members in a first pass, and then decide do some load balancing.
Also, even though each thread now writes data only at locations where noone else will write, the data may still belong to cache lines used by other threads, resulting in false sharing . For instance, in order increment cluster_member_count[2] , a thread need to get it from the memory since cluster_member_count 1 has just been modified by another thread. This is slow. A better way would be arrange that each thread only writes data to contiguous memory spaces. #pragma omp parallel
