A: Since i can't see you code i'll try to guess... For me that sounds a bit like a problem with nested loops when using #pragma omp for. In case you have nested loops you have to set the counter variables of inner loops as private. Take a look at this sample: #pragma omp for private(j)
for(i=0; i<100; i++)
{
    for(j=0; j<10; j++)
    {
       A[i] = A[i] * 2;
    }
} The variable j is set to private to have a instance of it in every thread, not the same instance for all threads. Check this out in your code, maybe that's the problem. And (your compiler should tell you that) don't use break; in your parallized loops. That won't work. Good luck!

