 for (i = 0; i < num_steps; i++)
 {
      x = (i + 0.5) * step;
      sum = sum + 4.0 / (1.0 + x * x);
 } Declaring the variable 'x' within the scope of the parallel for #pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum)
 for (i = 0; i < num_steps; i++)
 {
      double x = (i + 0.5) * step;
      sum = sum + 4.0 / (1.0 + x * x);
 } The final code could look like the following: #include <omp.h>
