A: For parallel programming you should also design your problem in a way such that you rarely need to sync your threads. Each time you sync your threads you will get the worst performance of all threads. If you need to sync your threads, try to redesign your problem, to avoid these syncs. Tweaking your code from #pragma omp parallel for to #pragma omp task won't get you any significant improvments, as their execution time difference is normally neglectable. Before trying to tweak some routine calls or omp statments you need to adapt your problem to parallel execution. You need really think in "parallel" to get a good and scalable performace increase, just adapting serial code rarely works. In your code you should try to parallize the while loop and not the inner for loops. If you parallize the small for loop you will not get any significant performance increase.
