A: I already went into detail on how to to this here Fill histograms (array reduction) in parallel with OpenMP without using a critical section It's the same as an array reduction.  OpenMP does not have built in support for this in C/C++ (but it does in Fortran) so you have to do it yourself. The easy solution is to create private version of the histogram, fill them in parallel, and them merge them into one histogram in a critical section.  In your case you can do that like this: int i, histogram[10];
for(i=0; i<10; i++) histogram[i] = 0;
#pragma omp parallel
{
    int i, j, histogram_private[10];
    for(i=0; i<10; i++) histogram_private[i] = 0;
    #pragma omp for nowait
    for(i=0; i<N1; i++) {
       for(j=0; j<N2; j++) {    
           histogram_private[img[i][j]]++;
       }
    }      
    #pragma omp critical 
    {
        for(i=0; i<10; i++) histogram[i] += histogram_private[i];
    }
} It's possible to merge in parallel as well but that's more complicated.  See the first link I mentioned for more details.
